## Implemented behavior

MoonPhaseTool retains its current reference UTC selection, C014 point-membership refusal, two primary full-engine Sun/Moon calls, full angle and illumination, and existing lite phase name. It removes private altLon, unused day-start/day-end resolutions and the two endpoint Moon samples. The exact longitude remains in the disclosure; the captured qualification is now a visible existing-style notice. Known-time/no-city UTC-conversion wording is shown visibly. Known-time/selected-city results retain their empty caption. Existing revision fences, pending-load handling, result/error focus and recovery are unchanged.

ChartCalculator changes only the unknown-time Moon-mode phase label (plus the corresponding comment). Its known-time label remains “Moon phase at birth.” Shared noTimeNotice and explanatory help use generic reference-position wording without a clock or zone claim; Inspector receives that notice through its existing catalog dependency. The two Explorer copy tables no longer assert noon or that every other planet's birth sign is certainly right.

Six Moon-page FAQ answers now distinguish a reference moment from a whole date; the additional English paragraph is corrected. Each existing FAQ source still feeds both visible and structured content. There are no layout/style/navigation changes.

Six share-card referenceTimeNote translations, two chart-sheet settings/provenance phrases and their option comment are corrected. The two server preview edits are strings only: no-angle settings and description. Route/query validation, response headers, privacy behavior, model shape, rendering logic and wire fields are untouched. PT/FR/IT exact-key translation counterparts were changed to keep their existing byte-parity contract. Root owns the generated i18n-additions.md refresh through the unchanged generator.

The UI catalogs retain exactly 420 keys. Three keys retire one-for-one: middayLocalCaption → referenceLocalCaption, middayUtcCaption → referenceUtcCaption, moonChangedNotice → moonPhaseAtReference. All old runtime uses are gone. The six previously existing known-time UTC captions are unchanged.

