## Qualifications

There is no verified full-date Moon range, complete local-date interval or new phase algorithm. The lite phase category and full-engine angle are separate existing algorithms; their known near-boundary disagreement remains explicitly open. Supplying a known time retains the existing civil gap/fold policy. The portable receipt's `reference: 'local-noon'` request convention and all wire/schema/API contracts remain unchanged.

Unrelated noon wording on home/birth-chart/methodology/glossary, compatibility, transit, solar-return and wallet surfaces remains separately tracked. Authentic noon timestamps in datasets, docs/examples, date-format anchors and request-selection code were not mechanically changed. Reference Sun downstream summaries remain the separately recorded boundary. This work does not claim those outputs are fixed.

The React skill checklist was applied as a source review: no new effects, state ownership, render-time imports or event listeners were introduced; captured result metadata remains owned by the existing run; the visible notice uses the existing live-status semantics. This is author review, not independent signoff. Independent review is being performed by the root-coordinated reviewers against the exact freeze.

Implemented and bounded-tested; not published, deployed or externally adopted by this author task.
